00:15:41,500 --> 00:15:45,559
Weather actually took the spears
and use them to capture the priests!

247
00:15:47,180 --> 00:15:49,020
He's within Weather's range!

248
00:16:02,040 --> 00:16:03,200
Did he get him?

249
00:16:05,380 --> 00:16:08,020
Don't do it, Weather.

250
00:16:08,480 --> 00:16:10,597
While you were in Green
Dolphin Street Prison,

251
00:16:10,680 --> 00:16:15,977
I could have finished you off at any
given moment if I truly wanted to except I

252
00:16:16,060 --> 00:16:20,777
had it in my head that one day I could save
you which is why I stole your memories.

253
00:16:20,860 --> 00:16:24,507
This isn't some convenient excuses
if I'm begging for my life.

254
00:16:26,840 --> 00:16:27,720
Prime numbers.

255
00:16:27,880 --> 00:16:28,797
Listen to me brother.

256
00:16:28,880 --> 00:16:30,397
I did all the wrong with you.

257
00:16:30,480 --> 00:16:31,310
Three.

258
00:16:31,393 --> 00:16:32,877
I've worked tirelessly towards my goal of

259
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:35,417
attaining the power so that
both of us can prosper.

260
00:16:35,500 --> 00:16:38,317
There must be someone who obtains
the power to reach heaven.

261
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:40,337
It was It's faded to happen eventually!

262
00:16:40,420 --> 00:16:41,250
Seven.

263
00:16:42,560 --> 00:16:43,390
Stop it, Weather.

264
00:16:43,473 --> 00:16:44,303
Eleven.

265
00:16:45,080 --> 00:16:45,910
Thirteen.

266
00:16:46,020 --> 00:16:48,373
This is not an end to both of our lives!

267
00:16:48,860 --> 00:16:49,690
Seventeen.

268
00:16:49,773 --> 00:16:50,940
This is just sad.

269
00:16:51,280 --> 00:16:54,398
The kind of evil that doesn't
even realize it's evil.

270
00:16:54,540 --> 00:16:57,011
It's the most disgusting kind of them all!

271
00:16:58,000 --> 00:16:58,830
Nineteen.

272
00:16:58,913 --> 00:16:59,920
Pooch is afraid.

273
00:17:00,160 --> 00:17:01,042
His expression.

274
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:06,417
There's fear and despair written
all over his face! Twenty-three. No.

275
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:08,040
Stop this weather!

276
00:17:08,380 --> 00:17:10,027
You are the one who's wrong!

277
00:17:10,600 --> 00:17:12,424
You're the cursed one, brother!

278
00:17:12,960 --> 00:17:15,277
I'm the man who kept you alive,
and this is how you remain!

279
00:17:15,360 --> 00:17:16,190
It's over!

280
00:17:16,273 --> 00:17:17,103
Die, Keicho!

281
00:17:23,680 --> 00:17:25,517
What the hell are you doing?!

282
00:17:25,600 --> 00:17:28,657
I thought I told you that if you
tried anything weird, I'd kill you!

283
00:17:28,740 --> 00:17:29,570
No, wait!

284
00:17:29,653 --> 00:17:31,777
There was a sudden cloud
of dust and then a stray

285
00:17:31,860 --> 00:17:33,877
nail or something stabbed
straight through the tire!

286
00:17:33,960 --> 00:17:35,901
It isn't my fault I lost control!

287
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:37,757
Shut up, he's close.

288
00:17:37,840 --> 00:17:39,437
Weather is somewhere nearby.

289
00:17:39,520 --> 00:17:40,461
The priest, too.

290
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:43,380
Although, something looks off outside.

291
00:17:44,260 --> 00:17:45,090
You're right.

292
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:49,713
I can't see very well, but there's
something strange covering up the road.

293
00:17:50,560 --> 00:17:51,390
Weather!

294
00:17:51,473 --> 00:17:52,697
I know you're close by!

295
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:54,460
Respond to me! Weather!

296
00:17:57,200 --> 00:17:58,920
What is going on out here?

297
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:01,037
What kind of crazy horror scene is this?

298
00:18:01,120 --> 00:18:04,060
I can sense the priest
moving around nearby.

299
00:18:04,740 --> 00:18:05,940
He's super close.

300
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:09,242
I need to find Weather
fast before it's too late.

301
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:12,437
I have a feeling that something
terrible is happening.

302
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:15,237
Is this wind being stirred
up by Weather's ability?

303
00:18:15,320 --> 00:18:17,737
Has that damn priest not
turned into a snail yet?

304
00:18:17,820 --> 00:18:19,300
I honestly have no idea.

305
00:18:19,560 --> 00:18:21,017
I only know that he's here!

306
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:22,220
Let's find him!

307
00:18:27,500 --> 00:18:28,330
Jolene!

308
00:18:28,413 --> 00:18:29,358
I just saw someone!

309
00:18:29,460 --> 00:18:30,401
He's over there!

310
00:18:31,120 --> 00:18:34,937
I don't know if it's weather or the
priest, but they're in that direction.

311
00:18:35,020 --> 00:18:37,373
Jolene, the wind's starting to disperse.

312
00:18:38,020 --> 00:18:40,680
Also, my body's turning back to normal.

313
00:18:42,360 --> 00:18:44,340
Does this mean...

314
00:18:50,260 --> 00:18:51,090
OUCHI!

315
00:18:52,420 --> 00:18:53,700
Hold on, Jolene!

316
00:18:53,940 --> 00:18:55,577
Our bodies and stands
still haven't recovered

317
00:18:55,660 --> 00:18:57,677
all the way from
transitioning into snails.

318
00:18:57,760 --> 00:19:00,397
We can't beat the priest now
in terms of power and speed.

319
00:19:00,480 --> 00:19:02,245
We have to find weather first.

320
00:19:02,460 --> 00:19:05,217
Well, if we beat the priest,
we can find weather, too!

321
00:19:05,300 --> 00:19:06,160
Stone Ocean!

322
00:19:09,100 --> 00:19:09,930
Join!

323
00:19:17,820 --> 00:19:19,380
What the? Weather!

324
00:19:20,740 --> 00:19:23,505
Nobody is capable of
catching up to me anymore.

325
00:19:23,700 --> 00:19:25,777
I suggest you enjoy the
rest of the days you

326
00:19:25,860 --> 00:19:28,331
have left with your family and loved ones.

327
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:30,894
Coming after me now is utterly useless.

328
00:19:31,220 --> 00:19:32,420
I always win.

329
00:19:34,860 --> 00:19:36,620
Don't do it, Jolene!

330
00:19:38,620 --> 00:19:39,450
Anastasia!

331
00:19:39,740 --> 00:19:41,900
This man is no longer the priest.

332
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:45,600
Who we know as Father Poochie
isn't here anymore. What?

333
00:19:48,140 --> 00:19:49,880
This is a revelation.

334
00:19:50,860 --> 00:19:52,154
That's not him either.

335
00:19:52,460 --> 00:19:53,957
It's one of his abilities.

336
00:19:54,040 --> 00:19:55,620
He made an afterimage.

337
00:19:58,060 --> 00:19:58,890
Versus!

338
00:19:59,340 --> 00:20:00,987
Using the cover of the wind,

339
00:20:01,080 --> 00:20:04,433
the priest planted a past
memory to this poor guy's head.

340
00:20:05,140 --> 00:20:08,258
He used his own ability to
craft an image of himself.

341
00:20:08,400 --> 00:20:11,360
The presence you were
feeling earlier was Versus.

342
00:20:12,200 --> 00:20:14,435
Pucci took this chance to execute him.

343
00:20:16,560 --> 00:20:18,240
This is a revelation.

344
00:20:18,780 --> 00:20:22,837
It would seem there's something on my
side that can only be classified as fate.

345
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:24,597
The threads of fate are
aiding me in reaching

346
00:20:24,680 --> 00:20:26,577
heaven in three days during the new moon.

347
00:20:26,660 --> 00:20:30,017
If it were not for destiny, I
would have surely been defeated.

348
00:20:30,100 --> 00:20:31,453
You believe in gravity.

349
00:20:31,540 --> 00:20:34,834
That is the reason why every
one of you came here today.

350
00:20:36,180 --> 00:20:37,010
Weather!

351
00:20:38,100 --> 00:20:40,340
I told you, it's not him.

352
00:20:40,540 --> 00:20:42,697
No one can pursue me! Can pursue me!

353
00:20:42,780 --> 00:20:44,160
Can pursue me!

354
00:20:47,960 --> 00:20:49,580
The snails are all gone.

355
00:20:49,820 --> 00:20:50,857
This is...

356
00:20:50,940 --> 00:20:52,528
Where's Weather, Anastasia?

357
00:20:53,180 --> 00:20:54,340
Where did he go?

358
00:20:54,720 --> 00:20:56,132
Hermes, did you see him?

359
00:20:56,780 --> 00:20:59,015
Can you not feel his presence anymore?

360
00:21:00,200 --> 00:21:02,729
You mean you really
can't tell where he is?

361
00:21:07,520 --> 00:21:08,350
Emporio!

362
00:21:14,160 --> 00:21:16,180
Hey, Yermis. He's there.

363
00:21:16,840 --> 00:21:17,800
Call a doctor.

364
00:21:18,040 --> 00:21:20,217
He should have healed
from the snails by now.

365
00:21:20,300 --> 00:21:21,130
Emporio!

366
00:21:21,213 --> 00:21:22,043
Jolene!

367
00:21:23,580 --> 00:21:24,440
I'm sorry.

368
00:21:24,680 --> 00:21:25,720
The wind stopped.

369
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:34,660
The rainbow disappeared too, Jolene.

370
00:21:41,380 --> 00:21:42,380
No way.

371
00:21:44,280 --> 00:21:45,600
It can't be.

372
00:21:46,020 --> 00:21:48,079
Is this because we crashed the car?

373
00:21:48,240 --> 00:21:50,240
Or is it because I came after him?

374
00:21:50,640 --> 00:21:51,470
But why?

375
00:21:53,760 --> 00:21:54,960
Listen, Jolene.

376
00:21:55,700 --> 00:21:58,229
Plenty of people have
called me a murderer.

377
00:21:58,400 --> 00:22:03,341
At least that's what the newspapers said
about me, and I don't necessarily disagree.

378
00:22:05,140 --> 00:22:10,100
When people asked me if I would sacrifice
myself for my family, I told them all no.

379
00:22:11,300 --> 00:22:14,006
I don't think my answer
would change even now.

380
00:22:14,240 --> 00:22:17,940
When it came to my parents, my
heart was never moved by them.

381
00:22:19,620 --> 00:22:20,450
However,

382
00:22:20,533 --> 00:22:22,537
I know I'd be willing to
risk my life for those that

383
00:22:22,620 --> 00:22:25,561
revived me from the dead
without a second thought.

384
00:22:26,100 --> 00:22:28,100
It was like that for Weather, too.

385
00:22:36,220 --> 00:22:37,050
That's...

386
00:22:37,460 --> 00:22:38,290
Yeah.

387
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:41,417
When Pale Snake was focused
on dealing the final blow,

388
00:22:41,500 --> 00:22:43,912
he took advantage of his special ability.

389
00:22:44,460 --> 00:22:47,660
He used that moment to seal
his ability into a disc.

390
00:22:50,320 --> 00:22:51,217
Hey, Jolene.

391
00:22:51,300 --> 00:22:53,660
I think Weather entrusted this to you.

392
00:22:59,400 --> 00:23:03,037
Weather came back to life when he
finally escaped from that prison.

393
00:23:03,120 --> 00:23:05,296
And that's the proof he left for you.

394
00:23:07,600 --> 00:23:10,660
In his final few days, he was happy.

395
00:23:11,720 --> 00:23:13,780
Weather had already been saved.

396
00:23:17,140 --> 00:23:17,970
Mother.

397
00:23:23,080 --> 00:23:24,440
One more time.

398
00:23:25,760 --> 00:23:27,520
I want to speak with you.

399
00:23:27,860 --> 00:23:29,440
Just one more time.

400
00:23:31,380 --> 00:23:32,760
Just once more.

401
00:23:33,680 --> 00:23:36,280
I want to talk to you in the soft breeze.

402
00:23:45,080 --> 00:23:46,480
Thank you.

403
00:24:13,780 --> 00:24:15,580
Thank you.
